;. /investigation_handoff_flow
  ;@ /flow/definition investigation_handoff
  ;= Hand an investigation to another participant
    Bind capture to an own-record inspection cell of the original work, using
    the raw cell path. Bind sources to a task brief and the cooperative-work
    guide. Add selected evidence to sources and cite it in the page briefs when
    a fuller handoff is needed. The original work may still be unresolved.
    This flow authors a handoff wiki; it never copies work into a new lifecycle.
    Its capture is an as-of snapshot, not a claim about current work status.

    ;@ /flow/input capture
    ;= Original work as an exact native capture
    ;@ /flow/input sources
    ;= Handoff brief and cooperative-work contracts

    ;@ /flow/step grounded ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/library/work_sources
    ;@ /flow/bind capture capture
    ;@ /flow/bind sources sources
    ;= Require native work while retaining its identity

    ;@ /flow/step handoff ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/revise
    ;@ /flow/bind pages document
    ;@ /flow/bind sources grounded
    ;= Author the handoff through the shared revision hand

    ;@ /flow/step pages ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/evidence
    ;@ /flow/bind pages handoff
    ;@ /flow/bind sources grounded
    ;= Keep handoff pages and source provenance together

    ;@ /flow/result pages
    ;= Handoff wiki

    ;@ /flow/page /
    ;@ /flow/uses native task cooperate
    ;= Continue this investigation
      State the question, explicit scope and original native work address.
      Label the captured version and as-of status. Separate completed actions,
      observations, interpretations and unresolved decisions. A root capture
      does not include every child event; do not reconstruct missing steps.
      Keep the original owner, attempts and work identity. This handoff document
      is a reading aid, not a replacement controller or transfer of authority.

    ;@ /flow/page evidence
    ;@ /flow/uses native task cooperate
    ;= Evidence and its limits
      Name only evidence and captures established by the supplied records.
      Distinguish retained facts from current live bindings. List unavailable
      event bodies, missing receipts and unanswered questions as explicit gaps.
      Link exact retained addresses when present. Never treat a deleted source
      as current because an earlier capture still exists. Do not infer that a
      model's summary proves a tool call or validation succeeded.

    ;@ /flow/page continue
    ;@ /flow/uses native task cooperate
    ;= Resume the same work
      Give a short ordered continuation plan grounded in the captured work.
      The next participant must reread the original controller, current holes
      and relevant evidence, then discover the declared answer, retry or resume
      action on that same subject. Use its current guards and hole generation.
      Supply the requested evidence or clarification; do not mark the work
      complete by editing a status field or writing into an attempt address.
      Name known owner and hole references; if the capture does not contain
      them, say what needs to be inspected instead of inventing paths. A flow
      definition or authority change requires explicit adoption. Preserve all
      old attempts and captures when a hand continues with the new evidence.
